# Hello, World!

Finally! After a few too many years of dicking around with the lovely thecasualdev.net domain 
I have made a website I am reasonably happy with. And I'm kinda pissed because this thing can't be more than like... 200 lines of code. 
(Shoutout to SvelteKit I guess).

Now it is by no means perfect.

But I have a game jam I wanna work on so it will do. I also hate CSS so don't expect this site
to work on mobile for atleast another couple of years. Unless I make like Epic Games and go for a full vibe codded project.


## Where to begin.
Genuinely not sure how to start, I never thought this day would come.

I suppose the important first step. Would be addressing why it took so long. And the simple truth
is I'm a bit of a perfectionist. Which sounds good in theory but in practice makes me shutdown the minute I'm not able to make something perfect.
It's part of the reason why I've not really released any project in the past... years... But I've been finally attempting some Game Jams. With the big one that started today
Unreal Epic AI MEGA JAM THING. Since I've not touched Unreal for 6 odd years I don't have much faith but I will tackle the challenge.

I want to test more stuff but It's getting late right now. So I'm off to bed.


